	(text "Battery chain (root sheet): J2 XT30 -> VBAT_IN -> F1 10 A MINI fuse -> VBAT_FUSED -> this sheet -> +12V.\nC36 (220 uF bulk, root sheet) is on +12V, after Q1, so a reversed battery can never reverse-bias it.\n\nQ1: high-side P-FET. A reversed battery leaves the body diode reverse-biased and VGS = 0, so nothing\ndownstream of Q1 ever sees negative voltage. Forward: about 7 mOhm, 0.2 W at 5 A.\nD12 limits |VGS| to 12 V (part limit 20 V); R36 holds the gate at GND.\nD13 (SMBJ16A) clamps fast spikes on +12V to about 26 V. It is NOT sized for motor regen if the BMS\ndisconnects (about 20 J); that must be clamped on the motor-driver side. If D13 fails short, F1 opens.\n\nVBAT_SENSE -> PA0 (ADC_IN0): VBAT = V(PA0) x 122.1 / 22.1 (5.525 x). 10.0 V -> 1.81 V, 14.6 V -> 2.64 V.\nLayout: Q1, D12, D13 between F1 and C36; D13 next to C36 with short, wide GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0ed29c42-12b8-4dfb-9096-3f09291f3d28")
	)
	(text "Input protection - reverse-polarity P-FET, gate clamp, TVS, battery sense"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects
